<%# The consent copy + privacy link of the AI opt-in.

    It lives under shared/ and no longer under ai_settings/ because the switch moved to
    the hub (doc/ki_zugang_umbau_plan.md D1/D8) — a partial rendered across folders is
    the kind of thing that reads as an accident later.

    ONE caller since that move, and one state: the ACTIVATION step. The active face of
    the switch is a status line with a privacy link and no long text (D2), so the two
    branches this partial once served are down to one. It stays a partial anyway: the
    copy is legally relevant, and its home should not depend on which view happens to
    render it today.

    text_class: tailwind classes for the paragraph (state-specific palette).
    link_class: hover/dark variants per palette — the plain hover:text-*-900
    shades are NOT remapped by the .dark wash shim (it only covers non-hover
    text classes), so each caller passes an explicit dark:hover: variant. %>
<p class="mt-2 text-sm <%= text_class %>">
  <%= t('views.organisations.ai_overview.activation.explanation') %>
  <%= legal_page_link :privacy,
                      label: t('views.organisations.ai_overview.activation.privacy_link'),
                      target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener',
                      class: "underline decoration-2 underline-offset-2 #{link_class}" %>
</p>
<%# S3 KI-Kontingent (DSGVO §4.3): purpose of the per-user usage attribution. %>
<p class="mt-2 text-sm <%= text_class %>">
  <%= t('views.organisations.ai_overview.activation.usage_note') %>
</p>
